I wrote `scorer_out.npz` and `NOTES.md` (194 words, from `wc -w`). The fix moves most wrong-exchange-rate complaints to fees_fx, but it is not complete.

**→ Results.** All numbers come from `write_out.py` in my scratch folder. I used forward passes only, through the official `scorer.py`.
- **Evidence:** 30/32 correct, up from 16/32. Two wrong-rate messages still go to disputes.
- **Held-out wrong-rate messages I wrote:** 26/30 now go to fees_fx.
- **Held-out other messages:** 39/40 and 16/16 unchanged.
- **General mixed set:** 84/85 unchanged.

**→ Risk: some foreign-currency messages also move.** In my difficult training sets, 7-11% move to fees_fx. Examples are "foreign currency payment declined" and "what rate applies to cash withdrawals". The base model already routes most of these by a margin under 0.6, so the hidden test will probably show some changes outside the correction.

**→ What I changed.** The original scorer weights stay the same. I added an extra ReLU module of 1024→9→1→1. It adds about +3 to the fees_fx logit only when four checks all pass:
- the option is fees_fx;
- the message is not a dispute;
- it is not a plain exchange-rate question;
- it is not about other currency topics.

Each check is a difference of means over messages I wrote. The module on raw vectors gives the same output as the exact rule to within 0.009 logits.

**→ Why it was hard.** Each marker vector is close to a single relevance score: two directions hold 99.5% of the variance. The useful content is in very small leftover directions, so simple directions did not work.

**→ Rules (borderline, so check).**
- I used SVD, with no labels, on my own messages to find the score directions.
- I used least squares one time as a diagnostic. No weight came from it.
- The thresholds are percentiles of my own messages. I did not use evidence labels.

Mistake: I let percentile thresholds pick inverted ramps, which fired on almost everything. Guard: the ramp builder now asserts low < high, and that assert then rejected three bad settings. This folder has no lessons file. I suggest `.work/review/MISSES.md` for the next steps.

**Also found:** I did not update the work board for this task.

**Next action:** run the hidden test on `scorer_out.npz`. If the "unchanged" score is too low, lower the boost from 3.0 to 2.5. On my sets that cut the flips, but held-out fixes dropped from 26/30 to 25/30.
